Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/libtests/timepng.c
Line: 552
Function: main
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: When reading filenames from stdin, if a line does not end with a newline (e.g., the last line without a trailing newline), the else branch prints an error using filename+len-32. If len < 32 (short line), this pointer underflows before the start of the filename buffer, and fprintf with %s reads from out-of-bounds stack memory, causing a stack OOB read and potential crash or information leak.

